# What regenerate.sh needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the only file that
# uses these tools. Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Olm's lib/deps.lua for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# All optional, because the picker searches a committed data.lua and works whether or not
# these are present. Only the refresh path fails without them, which is a maintenance task
# rather than a feature, so a missing one must not cost the spoon.
#
# regenerate.sh is a plain shell script run by hand from the repository, so it cannot reach
# the shared resolver and checks for these itself. That is the one probe in this module
# outside the door, and it is here because a script that runs without Hammerspoon has no
# door to use. It names the tools and stops there, the same rule every other file follows.
jq   | path | jq   | optional | reshaping both upstream sources into the vendored dataset
perl | path | perl | optional | parsing the Unicode Character Database into candidate rows
hs   | path | hs   | optional | rendering every candidate glyph to drop the ones that draw as a box, and writing the dataset
